-29)\n- Comparing the top 20 genes ranked independently by RNA nCPM and protein intensity, cardiomyocytes share 3 genes (TTN, MYH7, MYBPC3) with a union of 37 genes and Jaccard index of 0.0810811; hepatocytes share 1 gene (ALB) with a union of 39 genes and Jaccard index of 0.025641; and neutrophils share 0 genes with a union of 40 genes and Jaccard index of 0. (evidence: a98 row 0: cell_type=cardiomyocytes, overlap_count=3, jaccard_index=0.0810811, union_count=37; row 1: cell_type=hepatocytes, overlap_count=1, jaccard_index=0.025641, union_count=39; row 2: cell_type=neutrophils, overlap_count=0, jaccard_index=0, union_count=40 | a65 row 0: cell_type=cardiomyocytes, gene=TTN, ensembl=ENSG00000155657; row 1: cell_type=cardiomyocytes, gene=MYH7, ensembl=ENSG00000092054; row 2: cell_type=cardiomyocytes, gene=MYBPC3, ensembl=ENSG00000134571 | a67 row 0: cell_type=hepatocytes, gene=ALB, ensembl=ENSG00000163631)\n- The five genes per cell type with the largest absolute RNA-minus-protein percentile differences include: in cardiomyocytes, ALB (diff 98.0059, rna_pct 98.3029, protein_pct 0.296988; Main location: Endoplasmic reticulum;Golgi apparatus), PDZRN3 (diff 97.2210, rna_pct 0.975817, protein_pct 98.1969; Main location: Cytosol), ACTBL2 (diff 96.9877, rna_pct 98.3029, protein_pct 1.31523; Main location: blank), H4C15 (diff 96.2452, rna_pct 98.3029, protein_pct 2.0577; Main location: blank), and H4C6 (diff 96.2452, rna_pct 98.3029, protein_pct 2.0577; Main location: blank); in hepatocytes, EEF1A2 (diff 98.0785, rna_pct 98.4962, protein_pct 0.417711; Main location: Cytosol), H4C1 (diff 97.7778, rna_pct 98.4962, protein_pct 0.718463; Main location: blank), H4C8 (diff 97.2097, rna_pct 97.9282, protein_pct 0.718463; Main location: blank), H4C14 (diff 97.2097, rna_pct 97.9282, protein_pct 0.718463; Main location: blank), and SDHA (diff 95.6057, rna_pct 98.4962, protein_pct 2.89056; Main location: Mitochondria); and in neutrophils, TXNIP (diff 99.2031, rna_pct 0.648629, protein_pct 99.8517; Main location: Plasma membrane), H4C15 (diff 98.8881, rna_pct 98.9251, protein_pct 0.0370645; Main location: blank), H4C12 (diff 98.8881, rna_pct 98.9251, protein_pct 0.0370645; Main location: blank), H4C9 (diff 98.8881, rna_pct 98.9251, protein_pct 0.0370645; Main location: blank), and MYH7 (diff 98.1838, rna_pct 98.9251, protein_pct 0.74129; Main location: Focal adhesion sites). (evidence: a61 row 0: cell_type=cardiomyocytes, gene=ALB, ensembl=ENSG00000163631, rna_nCPM=0.1, protein_intensity=5446982731.6, rna_pct=98.3029, protein_pct=0.296988, abs_pct_diff=98.0059, Main location=Endoplasmic reticulum;Golgi apparatus; row 1: cell_type=cardiomyocytes, gene=PDZRN3, ensembl=ENSG00000121440, rna_nCPM=1323.3, protein_intensity=21502.8, rna_pct=0.975817, protein_pct=98.1969, abs_pct_diff=97.221, Main location=Cytosol; row 2: cell_type=cardiomyocytes, gene=ACTBL2, ensembl=ENSG00000169067, rna_nCPM=0.1, protein_intensity=941594818.8, rna_pct=98.3029, protein_pct=1.31523, abs_pct_diff=96.9877, Main location=\u2014; row 3: cell_type=cardiomyocytes, gene=H4C15, ensembl=ENSG00000270276, rna_nCPM=0.1, protein_intensity=604031635.6, rna_pct=98.3029, protein_pct=2.0577, abs_pct_diff=96.2452, Main location=\u2014; row 4: cell_type=cardiomyocytes, gene=H4C6, ensembl=ENSG00000274618, rna_nCPM=0.1, protein_intensity=604031635.6, rna_pct=98.3029, protein_pct=2.0577, abs_pct_diff=96.2452, Main location=\u2014; row 5: cell_type=hepatocytes, gene=EEF1A2, ensembl=ENSG00000101210, rna_nCPM=0.1, protein_intensity=1399549190.2, rna_pct=98.4962, protein_pct=0.417711, abs_pct_diff=98.0785, Main location=Cytosol; row 6: cell_type=hepatocytes, gene=H4C1, ensembl=ENSG00000278637, rna_nCPM=0.1, protein_intensity=970554190.6, rna_pct=98.4962, protein_pct=0.718463, abs_pct_diff=97.7778, Main location=\u2014; row 7: cell_type=hepatocytes, gene=H4C8, ensembl=ENSG00000158406, rna_nCPM=0.2, protein_intensity=970554190.6, rna_pct=97.9282, protein_pct=0.718463, abs_pct_diff=97.2097, Main location=\u2014; row 8: cell_type=hepatocytes, gene=H4C14, ensembl=ENSG00000270882, rna_nCPM=0.2, protein_intensity=970554190.6, rna_pct=97.9282, protein_pct=0.718463, abs_pct_diff=97.2097, Main location=\u2014; row 9: cell_type=hepatocytes, gene=SDHA, ensembl=ENSG00000073578, rna_nCPM=0.1, protein_intensity=274170335.0, rna_pct=98.4962, protein_pct=2.89056, abs_pct_diff=95.6057, Main location=Mitochondria; row 10: cell_type=neutrophils, gene=TXNIP, ensembl=ENSG00000265972, rna_nCPM=5229.1, protein_intensity=9773.7, rna_pct=0.648629, protein_pct=99.8517, abs_pct_diff=99.2031, Main location=Plasma membrane; row 11: cell_type=neutrophils, gene=H4C15, ensembl=ENSG00000270276, rna_nCPM=0.1, protein_intensity=7043887585.6, rna_pct=98.9251, protein_pct=0.0370645, abs_pct_diff=98.8881, Main location=\u2014; \u2026 3 more rows)\n\n**Limitations**\n\n- Absolute amounts, molecule copy numbers, and cross-assay molar ratios are not measured by the Human Protein Atlas and cannot be inferred from relative expression units (nCPM and Intensity).\n- Single-cell-type RNA sequencing and Deep Visual Proteomics sample different tissue cohorts and technological capture efficiencies, meaning differences in detection sensitivity and dynamic range contribute substantially to low genome-wide correlation.\n- Subcellular location annotations from immunofluorescence are absent or unannotated for several histone cluster genes (H4C family) and ACTBL2, which appear as blanks rather than confirmed absences.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- a1 data \"DVP protein intensity for 3 cell types\" (19297 rows) from investigator_hpa\n- a2 data \"Single-cell RNA nCPM for 3 cell types\" (20162 rows) from investigator_hpa\n- a3 data \"Subcellular location annotations\" (13603 rows) from investigator_hpa\n- a4 data \"select(artifact=a2, columns=[\"ensembl\",\"gene\",\"cardiomyocytes\"], \u2026)\" (20162 rows) from select of a2\n- a5 data \"select(artifact=a1, columns=[\"ensembl\",\"gene\",\"cardiomyocytes\"], \u2026)\" (19297